  {
   "id": 648392,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Use the following scenario to answer questions 1 – 3.</p>\n<blockquote>\n  <p>A water balloon is launched by a catapult into the air. The water balloon is launched from 4 feet above the ground, with an initial vertical velocity of 40 feet per second.</p>\n  <p>The function <span data-math=\"h(t)=-16t^2 + 40t + 4\">h(t)=-16t^2 + 40t + 4</span> models the height of the water balloon over the ground, in feet, <span data-math=\"t\">t</span> seconds after launch.</p>\n</blockquote>\n  <p><img alt=\"A DOWNWARD PARABOLA. X-AXIS LABEL IS TIME IN SECONDS AND Y-AXIS LABEL IS HEIGHT IN FEET. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS (0, 4), (0.5, 20), (1, 28), (1.5, 28), (2, 20), AND (2.5, 4).\" class=\"img-fluid atto_image_button_text-bottom\" height=\"272\" src=\"exercises/media/501e9621555c96b7.jpg\" width=\"260\"></p>\n  <ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\">\n    <li>What is the height of the water balloon 1 second after launch?</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1278573,
     "content_html": "34 feet"
    },
    {
     "id": 1278574,
     "content_html": "28 feet"
    },
    {
     "id": 1278575,
     "content_html": "22 feet"
    },
    {
     "id": 1278576,
     "content_html": "18 feet"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 648393,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\">\n  <li>Will the water balloon still be in the air 2 seconds after the launch?</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1278577,
     "content_html": "No"
    },
    {
     "id": 1278578,
     "content_html": "Yes"
    }
   ],
